# Firestorm Phoenix, a flyer, is dealt lethal damage by its own controller's Lightning Bolt in their first main phase.
# Instead of dying it returns to its owner's hand, not the graveyard (CR 614.1a, 700.4). Until that player's next turn they
# play with it revealed - the opponent sees it in their hand, on their own turn as well (CR 701.20a) - and can't cast it,
# though it is their main phase with the stack empty and mana to spare (CR 101.2, 701.18b). On the owner's next turn the
# card is hidden again and may be cast (CR 611.2a).

